# Build output
/target/
/dist/

# The Electron build's leavings. Its sources are gone from this branch, but a
# checkout that once built it still has these on disk, and they are not ours to
# carry. Kept as plain names rather than rooted paths so a nested one is caught
# too.
node_modules/
out/

# Real appliance archives, and the reason this line has always been here: they
# carry live encryption keys for real machines. crates/hcpd-core/tests/
# electron_parity.rs reads them when they are present and skips itself when
# they are not.
profiles-homeconnectdirect

# Fetched rather than committed. Both spellings: the tool was named without a
# suffix before it became architecture aware.
/packaging/linux/appimagetool
/packaging/linux/appimagetool-*

# makepkg's work, beside the PKGBUILD.
#
# The clone is the one to watch: `source=("$pkgname::git+file://...")` puts a
# bare repository next to the PKGBUILD under the package's own name, not under
# src/, and a `git add -A` swallowed all seventy-four files of it once.
/packaging/aur/src/
/packaging/aur/pkg/
/packaging/aur/homeconnect-profile-downloader/
/packaging/aur/*.pkg.tar.zst
/packaging/aur/*.tar.gz

# The comparison against the Electron version, kept local.
#
# It reads real appliance archives, which carry live encryption keys and are
# ignored two blocks up, so it can only ever run on a machine that has them.
# Committing tooling that nobody else can run would be committing a promise
# nobody else can check.
/tools/
/crates/hcpd-core/tests/electron_parity.rs

# The notes from porting, kept local for the same reason.
#
# Three measurement logs: the parity run, and what the application did in the
# Windows and macOS test VMs. All three describe machines that exist on one
# desk. They were worth writing while the port was in doubt and they are worth
# keeping, but they document the port rather than the program, and a reader of
# this repository cannot repeat a single line of them.
#
# doc/oauth-webview.md stays in, because the code points at it.
/doc/electron-parity.md
/doc/macos.md
/doc/windows.md

# Editors and desktops
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
